    "draft": false,
    "readyForModeration": false,
    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">The Mandelbrot set is famous for its endless detail: zoom anywhere on its border and new spirals, valleys and tiny copies of the whole set appear. Your goal is to explore it with a text console: given a rectangular <strong>box</strong> of the complex plane, draw it as <strong>ASCII art</strong>.<br><br><strong>The Mandelbrot set</strong><br>For a complex number c, repeat z = z&sup2; + c starting from z = 0. The point c belongs to the set when z never escapes to infinity. In practice, it is enough to check whether |z|&sup2; = re(z)&sup2; + im(z)&sup2; becomes greater than <const>4</const>.<br><br>With z = x + yi and c = a + bi, one step is:<br>x' = x&sup2; - y&sup2; + a<br>y' = 2xy + b<br><br><strong>Escape count</strong><br>For each point c, compute the escape count <var>n</var>:<br><pre style=\"font-family: monospace\">n = 0, z = 0<br>while n &lt; maxIter and |z|&sup2; &lt;= 4:<br>    z = z&sup2; + c<br>    n = n + 1</pre><br>So <var>n</var> is between 1 and <var>maxIter</var>.<br><br><strong>From points to characters</strong><br>The image has <var>W</var> columns and <var>H</var> rows. The character at column <var>col</var> (0 to <var>W</var>-1, left to right) and row <var>row</var> (0 to <var>H</var>-1, top to bottom) shows the point:<br>re(c) = <var>reMin</var> + <var>col</var> &times; (<var>reMax</var> - <var>reMin</var>) / (<var>W</var> - 1)<br>im(c) = <var>imMax</var> - <var>row</var> &times; (<var>imMax</var> - <var>imMin</var>) / (<var>H</var> - 1)<br>The four corners of the image are exactly the corners of the box, and the imaginary part grows upwards.<br><br>With a <var>palette</var> of <var>L</var> characters (indexed from 0):<br>- if <var>n</var> = <var>maxIter</var>, the point is considered inside the set: print the last character, <var>palette</var>[ <var>L</var>-1 ];<br>- otherwise, print <var>palette</var>[ <var>n</var> mod (<var>L</var>-1) ].<br>The escaping points cycle through the first <var>L</var>-1 characters, which draws bands around the set.<br><br><strong>Example</strong><br>With <var>maxIter</var> = <const>10</const> and <var>palette</var> = <const>.:-=+*#%@</const> (<var>L</var> = 9):<br>- c = 1: z goes 0 &rarr; 1 &rarr; 2 &rarr; 5. After the 2nd step |z|&sup2; = 4, which is not greater than 4, so a 3rd step is done; then |z|&sup2; = 25 &gt; 4. So <var>n</var> = 3 and the character is <var>palette</var>[3 mod 8] = <const>=</const>.<br>- c = -1: z goes 0 &rarr; -1 &rarr; 0 &rarr; -1 &rarr; ... and never escapes, so <var>n</var> = 10 = <var>maxIter</var> and the character is <const>@</const>.<br><br>Use 64-bit floating-point numbers (double) and the formulas above. The test cases are chosen so that the result does not depend on rounding errors.<br><br><strong>Fun fact</strong><br>This puzzle was inspired by a famous one-line C program that draws the set (it uses a slightly different algorithm, so it is not the specification):<br><br><pre style=\"font-family: monospace\">main(n){float r,i,R,I,b;<br>for(i=-1;i&lt;1;i+=.06,puts(&quot;&quot;))<br>for(r=-2;I=i,(R=r)&lt;1;r+=.03,putchar(n+31))<br>for(n=0;b=I*I,26&gt;n++&amp;&amp;R*R+b&lt;4;<br>I=2*R*I+i,R=R*R-b+r);}</pre><br><br><strong>References</strong><br>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandelbrot_set<br>https://people.sc.fsu.edu/~jburkardt/c_src/mandelbrot_ascii/mandelbrot_ascii.html<br>http://paulbourke.net/dataformats/asciiart/</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1</strong>: two space-separated integers <var>W</var> and <var>H</var>, the width and height of the image in characters.<br><strong>Line 2</strong>: four space-separated decimal numbers <var>reMin</var> <var>reMax</var> <var>imMin</var> <var>imMax</var>, the box of the complex plane to draw.<br><strong>Line 3</strong>: an integer <var>maxIter</var>, the maximum number of iterations.<br><strong>Line 4</strong>: a string <var>palette</var>, the characters to draw with.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><var>H</var> lines of <var>W</var> characters: the image of the box, from top (<var>imMax</var>) to bottom (<var>imMin</var>).</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">2 &le; <var>W</var> &le; 80<br>2 &le; <var>H</var> &le; 40<br>(<var>W</var> + 1) &times; <var>H</var> &le; 1000<br>-2.5 &le; <var>reMin</var> &lt; <var>reMax</var> &le; 1.5<br>-2 &le; <var>imMin</var> &lt; <var>imMax</var> &le; 2<br>1 &le; <var>maxIter</var> &le; 1000<br>2 &le; length of <var>palette</var> &le; 70<br><var>palette</var> contains printable ASCII characters, without spaces</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">40 12\n-2.2 0.8 -1.2 1.2\n30\n.:-=+*#%@</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">::::::::------=================---------\n::::::---===========++++**%+*#+++===----\n:::::--=========+++++*##%=@@@:%#**+====-\n::::-========+****##.*@@@@@@@@@@@*%*+===\n:::-==++++*#:#-@-::=@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@#+===\n:::++++##%:=#@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@%*++==\n:::++++##%:=#@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@%*++==\n:::-==++++*#:#-@-::=@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@#+===\n::::-========+****##.*@@@@@@@@@@@*%*+===\n:::::--=========+++++*##%=@@@:%#**+====-\n::::::---===========++++**%+*#+++===----\n::::::::------=================---------</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
